#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176826} :activity/id #uuid "8f647d7f-d10f-52b0-a5c4-c95324d956b1" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050269 :topic/id #uuid "3b1ff160-959d-503b-acf5-2be698a50baa" :topic/math-academy-id 3595} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176826 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186177047 :tutorial/content "Given a dataset of paired numerical observations $(x,y)$ and the corresponding linear regression model\n\n$$\n\\widehat{y} =f(x)\n$$\n\nthe **residual** for a particular observation $(x, y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nResidual &= Actual - Estimated \\\\\n&= y - f(x) \\\\\n&= y - y^(^)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe subtract the *estimated* value predicted by the model from the actual *observed* value.\n\nTo illustrate this concept graphically, consider the following example.\n\nThe owner of an ice cream shop keeps track of the average daily temperature $x$ (measured in $^\\circ \\mathrm{F}$) and the resulting daily ice cream sales $y$ (in dollars). The scatter plot for several randomly selected days and the corresponding linear regression line are shown below.\n\n![](images/fc/fc149b8d911a7a9863df9cc25c635d6155accd676e83e335a65d9083596b779b.png)\n\nSuppose the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny= 2.5 x +165\n$$\n\nLet's use our regression line to compute the residual of the point with coordinates $\\color{red}(82, 360)$ (shown in red on our graph).\n\nFirst, notice that since the highlighted data point has coordinates ${\\color{red}(82, 360)}$, our actual value is\n\n$$\ny = {\\color{red}360}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^(^) &= 2.5x + 165 \\\\\n&= 2.5(82) + 165 \\\\\n&= 370\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/38/3843c71b50251ae035378507ffb22cfade48dff8e1544d8e1317e4e6d611f7a1.png)\n\nFinally, we compute the residual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nResidual &= Actual - Estimated \\\\\n&= y - y^(^) \\\\\n&= 360 - 370 \\\\\n&=-10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe residual tells us that the linear model *overestimates* the true volume of ice cream sales by $\\[math]10$ when the outside temperature is $82^\\circ\\,\\textrm{F}$." :tutorial/id #uuid "7e5cd2f9-494e-5533-98e9-c24f42631dad" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5968 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "56d03218-9fd1-5cb5-a471-09641e54c0ea" :step/math-academy-id 36423 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176828}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176827 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176033 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175888 :question/id #uuid "bc4500bc-8992-5148-95eb-6f84ae2508cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-9717"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e77a14c-9943-5494-ae89-a77c7a1888d0" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049868}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176341} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176342} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524960} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525051}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining Residuals From a Graph"} :step/id #uuid "d5ff3834-5f43-5149-a054-8bfcbb8b3bbf" :step/math-academy-id 36424 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176829}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176828 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176034 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175889 :question/id #uuid "cb2190d0-5150-53ff-b7ab-ed364611bc8f" :question/math-academy-id "e-9718"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0286d36b-217f-52e4-8580-e031b6dea31e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050210}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176339} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176340}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing Residuals Using the Regression Line Equation"} :step/id #uuid "2dbc11bb-69e2-5610-9c8e-28e53d57e103" :step/math-academy-id 36425 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176827}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176829 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186177048 :tutorial/content "A **residual plot** displays the values of the independent variable along the horizontal axis and the residuals along the vertical axis.\n\nThe scatter plot below represents data from a four-day sample on the number of people visiting a swimming pool and the average daytime temperature, in degrees Celsius. The line $\\ell$ is the corresponding linear regression line.\n\n![](images/62/6228578012fac7e42bedeb7ab7ad5fc9f42432aed8d5751b675df560bc867417.png)\n\nThese residuals for each of the four data points are highlighted below:\n\n![](images/d7/d70c44fe7b8fce43a8962ac104651acced75e10598e865a3b3c80d09f16ce234.png)\n\nIf we calculate the numerical values for the residuals at each data point (from left to right), we get the following results:\n\n$$\n-4, \\quad 8, \\quad -8, \\quad 4\n$$\n\nTo compute our residual plot, we plot each $x$-value and its corresponding residual on some coordinate axes:\n\n![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "ddf8fe09-fc0b-546d-942f-17a086708a11" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5969 :tutorial/title "Residual Plots"} :step/id #uuid "e65742ab-c850-50fd-b1a4-0670ddc16c2b" :step/math-academy-id 36426 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176833}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176830 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176035 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175890 :question/id #uuid "3b40900e-ca06-5951-8261-aa13d8f966ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-9719"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa97e57a-70d8-5708-8b7d-fa05604a3f88" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176343} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176344} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233432}] :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Residual Plots"} :step/id #uuid "a7847754-3ac7-5ffa-af5a-838c5d3e8886" :step/math-academy-id 36427} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176833 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186177051 :tutorial/content "![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)\n\nWe should be aware of the following interpretations for residual plots:\n\n- Any point *above* the horizontal axis represents a *positive* residual. A positive residual means that the regression model *underestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n- Any point *below* the horizontal axis represents a *negative* residual. A negative residual means that the regression model *overestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n\nResidual plots can also be used to assess whether a trend line is a \"good\" fit for the corresponding data:\n\n- If a linear trend line is a good fit for the data, the residuals should be scattered randomly above and below the horizontal axis and be relatively close to zero.\n- In cases where the residuals show some clear pattern, this usually indicates that the data has no linear trend.\n\nThe residuals are scattered randomly about the horizontal axis in our last example. However, they are not close to zero, indicating that the trend line is a weak fit for the data." :tutorial/id #uuid "d7794124-93e8-5abb-8a78-4c8884a07547" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6034 :tutorial/title "Properties of Residual Plots"} :step/id #uuid "3fdb60d4-7e70-551a-9e4a-8bb61625c9cc" :step/math-academy-id 36805 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176830}}] :activity/title "Residuals and Residual Plots" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186176138}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525099} :activity/id #uuid "1565ea4e-c392-50d1-9414-12d443b010cf" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050269 :topic/id #uuid "3b1ff160-959d-503b-acf5-2be698a50baa" :topic/math-academy-id 3595} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525092 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524960 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "155561b0-11da-52be-a290-8bc7fd41e681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524422} {:answer/id #uuid "56a2ddd1-cadc-5a93-9a25-8dddff01f271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524532} {:answer/id #uuid "aefdfe8c-fa67-577b-98ee-259e0b602d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524663} {:answer/id #uuid "e0fe8d85-7874-5929-8753-4945ee9ab9ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524773} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a545ba-ef49-5db8-a0d9-0458f6933545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524778}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524773} :answer-field/id #uuid "48948107-5211-5ac2-9e2d-522c9771683b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "06429645-5834-5aa5-be8c-7530ab34a0e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134787" :question/problem "![](images/55/553af60aa28cbdd7565259eacc167187bc9c63a5b30cd78a6c14a3c43603fca2.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(5,3).$ So, our actual value is $y=3.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=5$ has the $y$-coordinate $5.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=5.$\n\n![](images/c5/c558c80b7056b794534146d3b99f399c3084806758f78bd6eddb39e8c89248e9.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =3-5 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4f48dbfb-61be-5cd7-8c7c-7f3723f848b5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525098}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525098 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525051 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "288479be-98bd-57e4-9608-f6f04980af8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524457} {:answer/id #uuid "a92e5308-f602-5b56-8117-08f3a63517ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524653} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7640de-088c-554a-a442-df97fc11d882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524720} {:answer/id #uuid "e5da0595-ab74-5f54-bd61-a8b4f9a3237a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524785} {:answer/id #uuid "ffffc3bb-9a0e-59c2-9d08-ba493528be35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524841}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524457} :answer-field/id #uuid "c15ed523-3e32-50d6-b2d3-15996b2f731b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e01898f3-3b5c-52d9-b3b4-b90e7c403824" :question/math-academy-id "q-134799" :question/problem "![](images/ae/ae35183698308f87acb254b7141d025bc55f815c49dea54231c713997c6a22eb.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(10,4).$ So, our actual value is $y=4.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=10$ has the $y$-coordinate $8.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=8.$\n\n![](images/61/61ed1ba4b285ac0d21410ddde91c3ed3882def52cbc500867aa7184114dd8fd8.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =4-8 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5cc55bd4-2c1a-5ba9-bb47-99a6d6d6d26a"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525099 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176341 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf731189-32fe-57a4-bde5-3c54274327ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174305} {:answer/id #uuid "1a6379b8-ece0-5a99-844b-b7f486334f38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174306} {:answer/id #uuid "441aa6e9-1299-567b-858c-691df1df7a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174307} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4cb6ac-32c3-5dd7-9a8f-634d8cdf9d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174308} {:answer/id #uuid "621b8204-3932-59dd-b595-a75ccb8e4c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174309}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186174308} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5802a2f-64ed-5fd4-b9cc-65c0cef24d68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dd98bac0-93e8-506d-a8ba-d1595548f912" :question/math-academy-id "q-134267" :question/problem "![](images/a7/a7fb89105bc5a11837ed0f416b2327d88202e8e782fa4c114ac47b3d5d15421c.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(7,-2).$ So, our actual value is $y=-2.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=7$ has the $y$-coordinate $-4.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=-4.$\n\n![](images/92/92a26b8ab019879dec3208878f6a0604c0616776b09e3f8fa916fcab72df3a73.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =-2-(-4) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "674c6b2d-1d05-59d6-90ed-5b152a4fab06" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525092}}] :activity/title "Residuals and Residual Plots" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524363}]}
